$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: 1-Oxaspiro[4.4]nonan-3-one (VIa). a. Dimethyl
sulfoxide, 58.5 g (0.75 mol), was added at -70°C to a solution of 47.6 g
(0.375 mol) of oxalyl chloride in 300 ml of anhydrous methylene chloride,
the mixture was stirred for 0.5 h, and a solution of 42.6 g (0.3 mol) of
compound Va in 200 ml of anhydrous methylene chloride was added at -70°C.
The mixture was stirred for 1 h, 80.8 g (0.8 mol) of triethylamine in 300
ml of methylene chloride was added, and the mixture was stirred for 0.5 h
at -70°C and for 10 h at room temperature. The dark organic solution was
washed with two portions of 20% aqueous citric acid, dried over anhydrous
sodium sulfate, and evaporated, and the residue was distilled under
reduced pressure. 1,8-Dioxaspiro[4.5]decan-3-one (VIf). Yield 83%. bp
84-86°C (1 mm), colorless oily liquid. IR spectrum: ν 1758 cm-1 (C═O). 1H
NMR spectrum, δ, ppm: 1.16-1.79 m (4H, CH2), 2.59 s (2H, CH2C═O), 3.61-
3.78 m (4H, CH2O), 3.92 s (2H, OCH2C═O). Found, %: C 61.38; H 7.45.
C8H12O3. Calculated, %: C 61.54; H 7.69.
