$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 75-09-2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Procedure for the Swern Oxidation
Using TAP-Supported DMSO 14. To a solution of oxalyl chloride (131 μL,
1.5 mmol, 1.5 equiv) in DCM (1.5 mL, 1M) at -40 °C was slowly added a
solution of TAP-DMSO 14 (1.49 g, 2.2 mmol, 2.2 equiv) in DCM(6.0 mL, 0.37
M). After 10 min, a solution of alcohol (1.0 mmol, 1.0 equiv) in DCM (2.5
mL, 0.4 M) was added and the solution was stirred at -30 °C for 1-2 h.
After 1-2 h, DIPEA (871 μL, 5.0 mmol, 5.0 equiv) was added and the
solution was stirred at -30 °C for 10 min and at rt for 30 min. The
solution was diluted with DCM (40 mL), washed with aq 10% (w/w) HCl (2 ×
5 mL) and water (5 mL), dried over Na2SO4, and concentrated under reduced
pressure. Celite (3.0 g) was added to the residue followed by slow
addition of Et2O (10 mL, over 1 min) to induce the complete precipitation
of the TAP-supported mixture of sulfide 13 and sulfoxide 14. The mixture
was filtered on Celite and concentrated under reduced pressure to afford
pure aldehyde.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM slow addition of phosphonium reagent solution stage 1, Swern oxidation
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tetraarylphosphonium Salts as Soluble Supports for Oxidative Catalysts
and Reagents
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Roy, Marie-Noelle; Poupon, Jean-Christophe; Charette, Andre B.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2009), 74(22), 8510-8515

