$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for Swern Oxidation of Derivatives 2 to
4-{2-[4-(ω-Oxoalkyloxy)Phenyl]Vinyl}Benzonitrile Derivatives 3. A
solution of DMSO (5.8 mL) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (97 mL) was added drop wise
under nitrogen to a cooled (-78°C), mechanically stirred solution of
oxalyl chloride (3.5 mL) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (97 mL). After a few
minutes, a solution of 2 (20.5 mmol) in anhydrous CH2Cl2 (70 mL) was
added drop wise and the mixture was allowed to stir for additional 40
min. at -78°C. After the addition of Et3N (14.3 mL), the mixture was
allowed to warm to rt, water was added and phases were separated. The
aqueous layer was extracted with CH2Cl2, and the collected organic phases
were washed several times with water and brine and eventually dried over
Na2SO4. After elimination of the solvent by rotary evaporation, crude
products were purified by column chromatography on silica gel using as
eluent 9:1 CHCl3/hexane (n = 6, 82%), 9:1 CH2Cl2/hexane (n = 7, 75%); 9:1
CHCl3/hexane (n = 9, 72%); 9:1 CHCl3/hexane (n = 11, 87%).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Swern oxidn., in-situ generated reagent in 1st stage
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM New liquid crystalline stilbene derivatives containing 1,2-dienylalkoxy
chains
