$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General Oxidation/Olefination Procedure B.
DMSO (650 μl, 9.15 mmol, 4 eq.) was added to a stirred solution of
(COCl)2 (400 μl, 4.57 mmol, 2 eq.) in CH2Cl2 (8 ml) at -78°C and the
resulting solution was stirred for 10 min. Diol 3a (300 mg, 2.29 mmol, 1
eq.) was then added as a solution in CH2Cl2 (7 ml) and the resultant
solution stirred for a further 30 min. Triethylamine (3.28 ml, 22.9 mmol,
10 eq.) was then added. After 2 h
(carbethoxymethylene)triphenylphosphorane (1.60 g, 4.57 mmol, 2 eq.) was
added as a solution in CH2Cl2 (15 ml) and the reaction mixture allowed to
warm to rt and stirred for 16 h. Aqueous saturated NaHCO3 (10 ml) was
then added, and the aqueous layer was separated and extracted with EtOAc
(4 × 10 ml). The combined organic extracts were dried (MgSO4), and
concentrated in vacuo to give the crude product. Purification by column
chromatography[eluting with 60% EtOAc in petroleum ether (40-60°C).
Ethyl-(E)-5,5-dimethyl-6-oxo-7-phenyl-hept-2-enoate 4d. (494 mg, 1.80
mmol, 82%) as a yellow oil. νmax (neat)/cm-1 2976s, 2935s, 1720s (C═O),
1654s, 1496m, 1468m, 1367m, 1191m, 1043m, 729s and 698s; δH (400 MHz,
CDCl3) 1.16 [6H, s, C(CH3)2], 1.21 [3H, t, J7.1 OCH2CH3], 2.37 [2H, dd,
J7.7, 1.2, CH2CHCH], 3.72 [2H, s, C(O)CH2Ph], 4.12[2H, q, J7.1, OCH2CH3],
5.76 [1H apparent d, J15.5, CHCHCO2,Et], 6.77 [1H, dt, J15.5, 7.7,
CHCHCO2, Et], 7.08 [2H, m, 2 × Ar o-CH], 7.19 [1H, m, Ar p-CH] and 7.24
[2H, m, 2 × Ar m-CH]; δC (100 MHz, CDCl3) 14.6 [OCH2CH3], 24.8 [2 ×
C(CH3)2], 42.2 [CH2CHCH], 44.2 [C(O)CH2Ph], 48.4 [C(CH3)2], 60.7
[OCH2CH3], 124.9[CHCHCO2Et], 127.2 [Ar p-CH], 128.9 [2 × Ar m-CH], 129.9
[2 × Ar o-CH], 134.7 [Ar C], 144.8 [CHCHCO2Et], 166.5 [C(O)O] and 211.6
[C(O)]; m/z (EI+ mode) 274 [(M+.) 15%], 229 (20), 183 (50), 155 (100),
127 (30), 109 (25), 91 (90), 81 (21), 55 (15), 41 (13); [Found: (M+.),
274.1572. C17H22O3 requires M, 274.1569].
