$DATUM B. With Pyridinium Dichromate. A solution of 21 (220 mg, 0.58 mmol) in
CH2Cl2 (25 mL) was treated with PDC (1.0 g, 2.66 mmol) and crushed 3 A
molecular sieves (1.32 g) and stirred at 23 °C for 24 h. At this time, an
additional 0.5 g (1.33 mmol) of PDC was introduced and the mixture was
agitated 48 h longer, diluted with ether, filtered through a silica gel
plug, and concentrated. Chromatography on silica gel (elution with 90%
ether in petroleum ether) furnished 0.18 g (82%) of 23.
