$DATUM Method B. Dess-Martin Oxidation A soln of alcohol 23 (3.71 g 10.0 mmol),
25 (4.47 g, 10.0 mmol), 31 (4.57 g, 10.0 mmol), or 32 (5.33 g, 10.0 mmol)
in anhyd CH2Cl2 (20 mL) was added dropwise to a stirred soln of
12-I-5-triacetoxyperiodinane (10.60 g, 25.0 mmol), solid NaHCO3 (1.6 g),
and molecular sieves (4 Å, 15 g) in anhyd CH2Cl2 (400 mL) at 0 °C under
an Ar atmosphere. After stirring for 4 h at r.t. (reaction monitored by
TLC), solids were filtered off, and the filtrate was concentrated. The
residue was purified by flash chromatography to provide the ethynyl
ketones 27,29,33, and 34.
1-(5-O-tert-Butyldimethylsilyl-2,3-O-isopropylidene-1-deoxy-β-D-ribofuranos-1-yl)pent-4-yn-3-one
(27) Method B. Purified by flash chromatography (solvent A8).
1-(5-O-tert-Butyldimethylsilyl-2,3-O-isopropylidene-1-deoxy-β-D-ribofuranos-1-yl)pent-4-yn-3-one
(27), Yield: 3.02 g (82%); colorless syrup [a]D24 -28.4 (c 1.0, CHCl3);
Rf = 0.25 (solvent A8). 1H NMR (300.13 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 0.05, 0.06 [2 x
s, 6 H, Si(CH3)2], 0.89 [s, 9 H, C(CH3)3], 1.33, 1.51 [2 x s, 6 H,
C(CH3)2], 1.83-2.05 (m, 2 H, H-1), 2.72 (m, 2 H, H-2), 3.21 (s, 1 H,
H-5), 3.69 (m, 2 H, H-5'), 3.85 (app dt, 3J1a,1' = 8.0 Hz, 3J1b,1' ≈
3J1',2' = 5.0 Hz, 1 H, H-1'), 4.00 (app q, 3J3'4' ≈ 3J4',5' = 3.5 Hz, 1
H, H-4;), 4.27 (dd, 3J2',3' = 6.6 Hz, 3J1',2' = 5.0 Hz, 1 H, H-2'), 4.62
(dd, 3J2',3' = 6.6 Hz, 3J3',4' = 3.5 Hz, 1 H, H-3'). 13C NMR (62.9 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = -5.5, -5.3 [Si(CH3)2], 18.3 [C(CH3)3], 25.5, 27.5 [C(CH3)2],
25.9 [C(CH3)3], 27.4 (C-1), 41.6 (C-2), 63.6 (C-5'), 78.5 (C-5), 81.3
(C-4), 81.9 (C-3'), 83.3, 84.5, 84.7 (C-1',2',4'), 114.0 [C(CH3)2], 186.3
(C-3). Anal. Calcd for C19H32O5Si (368.54): C, 61.92; H, 8.75. Found: C,
62.21; H, 8.93.
