$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: Oxidation of 1,2-Dimethanols II; General
Procedure: To a dry 500 mL three-necked flask equipped with a mechanical
stirrer, a thermometer and a dropping funnel, was added a solution of
CH2Cl2 (100 mL) and oxalyl chloride (8mL, 88 mmol) under dry Ar. The
stirred solution was cooled to -78 °C and a solution of DMSO (13.6 mL,
0.176 mol) in CH2Cl2 (25 mL) was added dropwise. The solution was stirred
for 3-5 min and 3-fluorobenzene-1,2-dimethanol (IIa, 6.2 g, 40 mmol)
dissolved in a CH2Cl2-DMSO mixture (10 mL) was added dropwise. The
reaction was allowed to continue for 0.5 h and then Et3N (100 mL, 0.71
mol) was slowly added at - 78 °C. The reaction mixture was allowed to
stir for 10 min and then slowly warmed to r. t. Ice-cold water (200 mL)
was added to the reaction mixture and the aqueous layer extracted with
CH2Cl2 (2 x 100 mL) and then dried (MgSO4). Removal of solvent gave the
crude dicarbaldehyde IIIa which was purified by column chromatography
using silica gel (grade 922, 200 mesh) and hexane-ethyl acetate (70:30)
as eluant and further purified by distillation. The procedure was
repeated for the preparation of other dialdehydes III.
ortho-Phthalaldehyde is a known compound. Analytical results of the other
dialdehydes are as follows. 4-Chlorobenzene-1,2-dicarbaldehyde (IIIb);
yield: 82%. bp 90-95 °C, mp 70-72°C (0.2 Torr). 1H NMR(CDCl3): δ = 10.52
(s), 10.45 (s), 7.96 (s), 7.93(d), 7.80(d). IR (KBr): v = 1695 cm-1
(>CO).
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Oxidation of aromatic 1,2-dimethanols by activated dimethyl sulfoxide
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Farooq, Omar
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
