$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Oxidation of 1,2-Dimethanols II; General Procedure: To a dry 500 mL
three-necked flask equipped with a mechanical stirrer, a thermometer and
a dropping funnel, was added a solution of CH2Cl2 (100 mL) and oxalyl
chloride (8mL, 88 mmol) under dry Ar. The stirred solution was cooled to
-78 °C and a solution of DMSO (13.6 mL, 0.176 mol) in CH2Cl2 (25 mL) was
added dropwise. The solution was stirred for 3-5 min and
3-fluorobenzene-1,2-dimethanol (IIa, 6.2 g, 40 mmol) dissolved in a
CH2Cl2-DMSO mixture (10 mL) was added dropwise. The reaction was allowed
to continue for 0.5 h and then Et3N (100 mL, 0.71 mol) was slowly added
at - 78 °C. The reaction mixture was allowed to stir for 10 min and then
slowly warmed to r. t. Ice-cold water (200 mL) was added to the reaction
mixture and the aqueous layer extracted with CH2Cl2 (2 x 100 mL) and then
dried (MgSO4). Removal of solvent gave the crude dicarbaldehyde IIIa
which was purified by column chromatography using silica gel (grade 922,
200 mesh) and hexane-ethyl acetate (70:30) as eluant and further purified
by distillation. The procedure was repeated for the preparation of other
dialdehydes III. ortho-Phthalaldehyde is a known compound. Analytical
results of the other dialdehydes are as follows.
3-Fluorobenzene-1,2-dicarbaldehyde (IIIa), yield 81%. bp 75-80°C (0.2
Torr). 1H NMR (CDCl3): δ = 10.55 (s), 10.52 (s), 8.04 (m), 7.81 (m), 7.75
(d). IR (KBr): v = 1700 cm-1 (> CO).
