$DATUM 2-Ethyl-3-oxocyclopent-1-enecarbaldehyde, 9. To a cooled (-78ºC) solution
of oxalyl chloride (160 μL, 1.85 mmol) in 12 mL of dry dichloromethane
was added DMSO (260 μL, 3.72 mmol) dropwise; the mixture was stirred at
this temperature for 30 min. Then, a solution of alcohol 7 (130 mg, 0.93
mmol) in 5 mL of dry dichloromethane was added dropwise via cannula, and
the resulting solution was stirred at -78 ºC for an additional 1 h.
Finally, 680 μL of triethylamine were added dropwise. After 2 h stirring
at -78 ºC, the reaction mixture was allowed to warm to room temperature
slowly. The reaction was quenched by addition of water and, after a few
minutes stirring vigorously, the layers were separated and the aqueous
layer was extracted with dichloromethane. The combined organics layers
were washed with brine, dried over anhydrous MgSO4, and evaporated. Flash
chromatography (4:6 hexanes/ethyl acetate) afforded 95 mg (78%) of 9 as a
colourless oil. IR (film): υmax 2928, 2845, 1716, 1668, 1213 cm-1. 1H NMR
(400 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.17 (t, J = 7.6 Hz, 3H, CH3), 2.48-2.58 (m, 2H,
CH2), 2.62 (q, J = 7.6 Hz, 2H, CH2), 2.67-2.71 (m, 2H, CH2), 10.41 (s,
1H) ppm. 13C-NMR (100 MHz, CDC3): δ 14.4 (CH3), 16.5 (CH2), 23.5 (CH2),
34.3 (CH2), 155.5 (C), 158.5 (C), 190.4 (C), 210.2 (C) ppm. MS (ESI (+)
H2O: CH3CN): m/z 139.1 [(M + H)+, 100%]. HMRS (ESI (+) H2O: CH3CN): calcd
for C8H11O2 : 139.0759; found: 139.0761.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
