$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedures for the formation of α-Halo Ketones A flame-dried
flask was charged with dry CH2Cl2 and cooled to -78°C with a dry
ice/acetone bath. Oxalyl chloride or oxalyl bromide (3 equiv) was then
added followed by DMSO (4 equiv). The reaction was kept at -78°C for 15
min, after which time the allylic alcohol (1 equiv dissolved in CH2Cl2)
was added. After addition of the allylic alcohol the concentration of the
reaction was approximately 0.1 M in regards to the allylic alcohol. The
reaction was kept at -78°C for 1 h, after which time triethylamine (6
equiv) was added and the reaction allowed to warm to room temperature
over 30 min. The reaction mixture was then poured over ice-cold 1M HCl
and extracted with hexanes. The combined extracts were dried (Na2SO4) and
concentrated. Purification of the residue by silica gel chromatography
provided the halogenated vinyl ketones or allylic chloride. 6 TLC Rf =
0.42 (10% ethyl acetate/hexanes); IR (film from CH2Cl2) 3065, 1672, 1597
cm-1; 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3) δ 7.78-7.84 (m, 2H), 7.45-7.60 (m, 1H),
7.44-7.50 (m, 2H), 6.54 (d, J = 2.4 Hz, S 4 1H), 6.47 (d, J = 2.4 Hz,
1H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3) δ 190.4, 135.3, 133.4, 130.4, 129.9, 129.8,
128.7. Anal calcd for C9H7BrO: C, 51.22; H, 3.34. Found: C, 51.30; H,
3.23.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM green chemistry (process simplification), Moffatt-Swern conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Tandem Oxidation/Halogenation of Aryl Allylic Alcohols under
Moffatt-Swern Conditions
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Yin, Jiandong; Gallis, Christina E.; Chisholm, John D.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2007), 72(18), 7054-7057

$RFMT $RIREG SCHEME202 STEP1
