$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: GP 4: Dess-Martin Oxidation The alcohol (1
equiv.) is dissolved in CH2Cl2 (50 mL per mmol alcohol), and stirred at
rt with Dess-Martin periodinane (2 equiv.) until the starting material is
consumed (TLC, 30-120 min). Then a solution of Na2S2O3 (5 g per mmol
alcohol) in satd. aq. NaHCO3 solution (50 mL per mmol alcohol) is added
and the mixture is stirred until both phases are clear (10-60 min). The
aqueous layer is extracted with twice the amount of CH2Cl2 (3 ×), dried
with MgSO4, and the solvent is removed under vacuum (25°C for the
synthesis of aldehydes). Methyl
(4S,4'S,4''R,5R,5'R)-5-[(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)amino]-4-methoxy-5-
(2',2',2'',2''-tetramethyl-4',4''-bi-1,3-dioxolan-5'-yl)-2-oxopentanoate
(27) and Methyl
(4S,4'S,4''R,5R,5'R)-1-(tert-Butoxycarbonyl)-2-hydroxy-4-methoxy-5-(2',2',2'',2''-tetramethyl-4',4''-bi-1,3-dioxolan-5'-yl)-D-prolinate
and -L-prolinate (28): Alcohol 121 (119 mg, 0.250 mmol) was dissolved in
CH2Cl2 (12 mL) and treated with Dess-Martin periodinane (212 mg, 0.500
mmol) as described in GP 4 (30 min). The yellow oil was purified by
column chromatography (silica gel, hexane/EtOAc = 5:2) to give 27 (92 mg,
77%) as a colorless solid and 28 (9 mg, 8%, dr = 53:47) as a yellow oil.
27: m.p. 76-77°C. [α]D21 = +6.7 (c = 1.0, CHCl3). 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 1.34 (s, 3 H, CMe2), 1.398 (s, 9 H, CMe3), 1.402, 1.41, 1.46
(3 s, 9 H, CMe2), 3.06, 3.12 (AB-part of an ABX-system, JAB = 18.3 Hz,
JAX = 6.1 Hz, JBX = 8.1 Hz, 2 H, 3-H), 3.42 (s, 3 H, OMe), 3.70 (ddd, J =
1.5, 9.4, 10.2 Hz, 1 H, 5-H), 3.87 (s, 3 H, CO2Me), 3.88 (dd, J = 4.1,
8.7 Hz, 1 H, 4'-H), 3.89 (dd, J = 6.0, 8.6 Hz, 1 H, 5''-H), 4.01 (td, J =
6.0, 8.7 Hz, 1 H, 4''-H), 4.10 (dd, J = 4.1, 10.2 Hz, 1 H, 5'-H), 4.14
(dd, J = 6.0, 8.6 Hz, 1 H, 5''-H), 4.16 (ddd, J = 1.5, 6.1, 8.1 Hz, 1 H,
4-H), 4.94 (br d, J = 9.4 Hz, 1 H, NH) ppm. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ =
25.3, 26.6, 27.6, 28.1 (4 q, CMe2), 28.2 (q, CMe3), 39.8 (t, C-3), 52.9
(q, CO2Me), 55.6 (d, C-5), 58.3 (q, OMe), 67.5 (t, C-5''), 74.8 (d, C-4),
77.1 (d, C-4''), 77.9 (d, C-5'), 79.7 (s, CMe3), 80.7 (d, C-4'), 109.6,
110.9 (2 s, CMe2), 156.2 (s, C=O), 160.9 (s, C-1), 191.8 (s, C-2) ppm. IR
(KBr): ν = 3450, 3365 (N-H), 2985-2830 (C-H), 1755, 1735, 1710, 1505
(C=O, H-NC=O) cm-1. C22H37NO10 (475.5): calcd. C 55.57, H 7.84, N 2.95;
found C 55.57, H 7.56, N 2.71. 28: Analyzed from a mixture dr = 53:47 (1H
NMR): IR (KBr): ν = 3500-3390 (O-H), 2985-2855 (C-H), 1750, 1710 (C=O,
NC=O) cm-1. MS (EI, 80 eV, 70 °C): m/z (%): 475 (2) [M]+, 460 (5) [M -
CH3]+, 399 (6), 386 (8), 342 (9), 316 (24), 274 (15) [M - C5H9O2 -
C5H8O2]+, 256 (25), 230 (15), 174 (100) [M - C5H9O2 - C5H8O2 - Boc + H]+,
143 (52), 101 (18) [C5H9O2]+, 57 (23) [CMe3]+. HRMS (EI, 80 eV, 70°C):
calcd. for C21H34NO10 [M - CH3]+ 460.2183; found 460.2177. Major isomer:
1H NMR (500 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.33-1.51 (m, 21 H, CMe2, CMe3), 2.34 (dd, J
= 11.5, 13.3 Hz, 1 H, 3-H), 2.51 (dd, J = 7.4, 13.3 Hz, 1 H, 3-H), 3.40
(s, 3 H, OMe), 3.80 (s, 3 H, CO2Me), 3.93-3.97 (m, 1 H, 5''-H), 4.07-4.19
(m, 4 H, 4-, 4'-,4''-,5''-H), 4.31-4.37 (m, 2 H, 5-,5'-H) ppm; OH-signal
could not be detected. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 25.3-27.4 (4 q,
CMe2), 28.1 (q, CMe3), 41.5 (t, C-3), 53.0 (q, CO2Me), 58.2 (q, OMe),
58.4 (d, C-5), 66.6 (t, C-5''), 77.2 (d, C-4''), 77.5 (d, C-5'), 78.7 (d,
C-4), 79.8 (d, C-4'), 81.9 (s, CMe3), 86.4 (s, C-2), 109.5, 109.9 (2 s,
CMe2), 153.1 (s, NC=O), 172.5 (s, C=O) ppm. Minor isomer: 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.33-1.51 (m, 21 H, CMe2, CMe3), 2.29 (dd, J = 11.5,
13.7 Hz, 1 H, 3-H), 2.54 (dd, J = 7.1, 13.7 Hz, 1 H, 3-H), 3.41 (s, 3 H,
OMe), 3.82 (s, 3 H, CO2Me), 3.93- 3.97 (m, 1 H, 5''-H), 4.07-4.19 (m, 4
H, 4-, 4'-,4''-,5''-H), 4.43-4.48 (m, 2 H, 5-,5'-H) ppm; OH-signal could
not be detected. 13C NMR (125 MHz, CDCl3): δ = 25.3-27.4 (4 q, CMe2),
28.1 (q, CMe3), 43.3 (t, C-3), 53.0 (q, CO2Me), 58.2 (q, OMe), 58.9 (d,
C-5), 66.4 (t, C-5''), 77.4 (d, C-4''), 77.5 (d, C-5'), 78.0 (d, C-4),
79.8 (d, C-4'), 81.9 (s, CMe3), 86.0 (s, C-2), 109.6, 109.9 (2 s, CMe2),
153.7 (s, NC=O), 172.1 (s, C=O)ppm. Due to the relatively small
difference in concentration, some of the 1H and 13C NMR signals from main
and minor product might be transposed.
