$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM GP 4: Dess-Martin Oxidation The alcohol (1 equiv.) is dissolved in CH2Cl2
(50 mL per mmol alcohol), and stirred at rt with Dess-Martin periodinane
(2 equiv.) until the starting material is consumed (TLC, 30-120 min).
Then a solution of Na2S2O3 (5 g per mmol alcohol) in satd. aq. NaHCO3
solution (50 mL per mmol alcohol) is added and the mixture is stirred
until both phases are clear (10-60 min). The aqueous layer is extracted
with twice the amount of CH2Cl2 (3 ×), dried with MgSO4, and the solvent
is removed under vacuum (25°C for the synthesis of aldehydes). Methyl
5-(Acetylamino)-3,5-didesoxy-4-O-methyl-6,7-O-(1-methylethyliden)-L-arabino-hept-2-ulosonate
(9) and Methyl
(4S,4'R,5R)-1-Acetyl-5-(2',2'-dimethyl-1,3-dioxolan-4'-yl)-2-hydroxy-4-methoxy-D-prolinate
and -L-prolinate (10): Alcohol 8 (27 mg, 0.085 mmol) in CH2Cl2 (4 mL) was
treated with Dess-Martin periodinane (72 mg, 0.17 mmol) as described in
GP 4 (1 h) to give 9 (19 mg, 70%) with small impurities as a yellow oil.
One of the impurities, for which we propose structure 10, 9: 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.36, 1.46 (2 s, 6 H, CMe2), 2.02 (s, 3 H, O=CMe), 2.92
(dd, J = 5.9, 18.0 Hz, 1 H, 3-H), 3.11 (dd, J = 6.8, 18.0 Hz, 1 H, 3-H),
3.44 (s, 3 H, OMe), 3.85 (dd, J = 4.9, 8.1 Hz, 1 H, 7-H), 3.88 (s, 3 H,
CO2Me), 3.98 (ddd, J = 1.0, 9.0, 9.6 Hz, 1 H, 5-H), 4.01 (dd, J = 5.8,
8.1 Hz, 1 H, 7-H), 4.02-4.06 (m, 1 H, 6-H), 4.24 (ddd, J = 1.0, 5.9, 6.8
Hz, 1 H, 4-H), 5.74 (br d, J = 9.6 Hz, 1 H, NH) ppm. 13C NMR (100 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 23.3 (q, O=CMe), 25.6, 26.8 (2 q, CMe2), 41.1 (t, C-3), 53.1
(q, CO2Me), 54.7 (d, C-5), 59.0 (q, OMe), 67.5 (t, C-7), 74.4 (d, C-4),
74.9 (d, C-6), 109.8 (s, CMe2), 161.0 (s, C-1), 170.3 (s, C=O), 191.8 (s,
C-2) ppm. MS (pos. ESI, in methanol): m/z (%): 372 (49) [M + MeOH + Na]+,
356 (4) [M + K]+, 350 (3) [M + MeOH + H]+, 340 (100) [M + Na]+. MS (pos.
ESI, in acetonitril): m/z (%): 657 (35) [2 M + Na]+, 356 (11) [M + K]+,
340 (100) [M + Na]+. HRMS (pos. ESI): calcd. for C14H23NNaO7 [M + Na]+
340.1367; found 340.1378.10: The NMR spectra were determined from a
mixture of 9 and 10. Missing signals could not be assigned unambiguously
or overlap with those of another compound. Major isomer: 1H NMR (500 MHz,
CDCl3): δ = 1.35, 1.41 (2 s, 6 H, CMe2), 1.79 (dd, J = 11.3, 13.8 Hz, 1
H, 3-H), 2.23 (s, 3 H, O=CMe), 2.51 (dd, J = 7.5, 13.8 Hz, 1 H, 3-H),
3.40 (s, 3 H, OMe), 3.78 (s, 3 H, CO2Me) ppm. Minor isomer: 1H NMR (500
MHz, CDCl3): δ = 1.88 (dd, J = 11.9, 12.5 Hz, 1 H, 3-H), 2.25 (s, 3 H,
O=CMe), 2.40 (dd, J = 6.3, 12.5 Hz, 1 H, 3-H), 3.44 (s, 3 H, OMe), 3.81
(s, 3 H, CO2Me) ppm.
